2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1029) 'Three removed models get permissive replacements, MIT or BSD.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1029) 'RFD66606-1028 removes three models from the catalog on its license gate, and their tasks still need a model.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1029) 'Check a replacement against the license gate in RFD66606-1028 before you adopt it. Its candidates and licenses are below.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1029) 'FOSS model replacements
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1029) 'Replace each deleted model with a permissive alternative. Prefer the MIT license and the BSD license.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1029) 'See `DETAILS.md` for the PartField, FastMesh, and PartPacker replacements, each with its candidates and its license.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1029) 'RFD66606-1028 records the license gate. RFD66606-1031 records the geometry refinement path and its alpha wrap problem.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1029) 'PartField replacement (mesh segmentation)
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1029) 'The web search from August 2026 found three MIT candidates.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1029) '- PartSAM (czvvd/PartSAM, ICLR 2026) segments parts on native 3D data. It supports a segment-every-part mode.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1029) '- HoloPart (VAST-AI/Research) completes occluded parts.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1029) '- OmniPart (HKU-MMLab, SIGGRAPH Asia 2025) does part-aware 3D generation.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1029) 'PartSAM is the primary recommendation. It trains on native 3D data, so it works on AI-generated meshes. PartField needs clean mesh connectivity, which generated meshes lack.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1029) 'FastMesh replacement (retopology)
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1029) 'The catalog already carries Instant Meshes under the BSD-3 license. It is the primary replacement. QuadriFlow, meshoptimizer, trimesh_decimate, and AutoRemesher are the MIT alternatives.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1029) 'The QuadWild Bi-MDF fork does not qualify. It uses the GPL-3 license.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1029) 'Two of the candidates are already vendored
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1029) 'Checked 2026-09-12. &{repo("entities-godot")} on `feat/cassie` carries both PMP and Geogram under `thirdparty/`, so the decimation half of this replacement is checked out rather than sourced. Licenses were read from those copies, not from a package index.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1029) '| library | license as vendored                                     |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

